# x86_64 FP Selector Foundation Evidence

schema_version: 1
directive: `INBOX-17`
target: `x86_64-linux-gnu`
validation_tier: 3
result: pass

The composed selector now models `half`, `float`, and `double` with independent
FP virtual classes and width-tagged XMM/spill locations. GPR and XMM occupancy
are separate; FP values retain the existing authoritative value map and frame
indexes. Live XMM values spill before calls, low-width values use the existing
32-bit XMM frame operations, doubles use the 64-bit operations, and supported
returns materialize in XMM0. `x86_fp80` and `fp128` remain fail-closed.

Focused evidence:

- `zig build test`: green, including a bit-exact executable half ABI round trip
  over zero, finite signed values, infinity, and a NaN payload.
- `zig build distribution-debug-object`: green.
- compiler-rt report-all: 443 selected / 163 emitted / 280 failed; first
  failure remains `compiler_rt.trunc.__trunch` and advances from
  `unsupported_type / unsupported-return-type` to
  `unsupported_instruction / fpext`.
- report log: `tmp/inbox17_foundation_report.log`.

Tier-3 trigger: shared SysV ABI classification, composed register allocation,
call clobbering, and frame spill behavior changed. Existing Tier-3 logs predate
these relevant inputs and cannot be reused.

Tier-3 command and intended output:

```text
zig build distribution-all
docs/evidence/distribution_all_after_fp_selector_foundation.summary
```

Tier 3 passed with 17 subgates and `local_fail=0`. The strict ReleaseFast,
ReleaseSafe, and ReleaseSmall 100-row gates passed, as did the integrated
object, executable, native-link, and boundary gates.
